      "pali": "Ajjhattapaccuppannayadaniccasutta ",
      "english": "The Interior and What’s Impermanent in the Present "
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "pali": "“Cakkhu, bhikkhave, aniccaṁ paccuppannaṁ. ",
      "english": "“Mendicants, in the present the eye, ear, nose, tongue, body, and mind are impermanent. "
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "pali": "Yadaniccaṁ, taṁ dukkhaṁ. ",
      "english": "What’s impermanent is suffering. …” "
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "pali": "Yaṁ dukkhaṁ, tadanattā. ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "pali": "Yadanattā taṁ ‘netaṁ mama, nesohamasmi, na meso attā’ti evametaṁ yathābhūtaṁ sammappaññāya daṭṭhabbaṁ …pe… ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
